On 4 Jun 2006 13:30:18 -0700, verdant75 wrote:

>Any possibility of having an artifact lance added to the game in a
>future release?  

  I don't think so.  XL 14 Knights with the Magic Mirror of Merlin casting the
spell of magic missile average 56 points of damage per hit per monster, and at
range.  (Grayswandir maxes out at 45 or so, under very restricted conditions.)

>I like jousting but in the mid to end-game, there's
>little reason to use a lance over other artifact weapons.

  I don't think you've done the damage calculations on that.  Expert jousting's
average +9 damage beats Grayswandir's damage for Knights except at +7
enchantment.  The knockback effect of jousting also looks like perfect defense.
(There's little better in NetHack than hitting a monster without getting hit
back.)

  At max skill, with 18 strength and +0 enchantment Knights do 12 damage with
Grayswandir.  (Yes, 12.)  Add in +2 for Expert riding skill and that's 14.  The
+0 lance in the same conditions with Expert skill would be doing 19, with
knockbacks.

                       Weapon   Riding  18 Str  Joust    Total
              Base     Skill    Skill   Bonus   (@80%)
Grayswandir   2x(4.5)    +1       +2      +2      +0      14
Lance          4.0       +2       +2      +2      +9      19


  Only at +7 is Grayswandir slightly better than the lance: 28 vs 26
(Or 32 vs 30 at max strength.)

  Grayswandir's not guaranteed.  Nor are the scrolls to enchant it.  The lance
is guaranteed.  A lance can always be wished for, guaranteed.  Not so
Grayswandir.

  That doesn't take into account 'a'pplying the lance at range 2.  Vs. slower
monsters joust, apply lance vs thrown-back monster, repeat.  Against faster
monsters joust means they'll spend their moves getting back into joust range.
Reduces the amount of damage taken vs. using Grayswandir.

  So there are reasons to use a lance over artifact weapons, at least for a
Knight who wants to do more damage while taking less damage.  Unfortunately the
many downsides still make it unreasonable.  (Hence the effects Magic Mirror of
Merlin giving a long-range lance.  Think of the 2x damage as doubling your
effective mana points.)




